124:We consider a relaxation of this problem in which the edges of $G$ can be drawn as a polygonal path consisting of at most two line segments.  Such a drawing is called a \defin{one-bend} drawing of $G$. A subset $Y$ of $V(G)$ is a \defin{one-bend free set} if, for every $|Y|$-point set $P$,  $G$ has a one-bend drawing in which the vertices of $Y$ are mapped to the points in $P$.  We show that, for any spanning tree $T$ of $G$, the leaves of $T$ are a one-bend free set of $G$.  Combined with \cref{main_theorem_cor}, this gives:
